"""Trace Parquet serialisation, ``trace_schema_version = 1`` with zstd (docs/11 §6.2).

One row per sample. Every column carries its unit in the Arrow field metadata (``unit``). File-level
metadata holds JSON-encoded values for ``trace_schema_version``, ``goal_x``, ``goal_y`` and ``meta``
(the whole :attr:`Trace.meta`). ``run_id``, ``backend`` and ``sample_hz`` are copied from ``meta``
when present, so tools can read them without decoding ``meta``. ``rtf`` is nullable; a trace
without RTF samples is written as all-null and read back as ``None``.

The module depends only on pyarrow and numpy, so the ROS ``episode_recorder`` can reuse
:data:`TRACE_SCHEMA`.

Implements: FR-RUN-004
"""

